<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44270" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐκολία</span></b> , ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔκολος</span>) prop. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>contentedness with one's food</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.461c
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ περὶ τὴν δίαιταν εὐ</span>.
				<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Caes.</u>
				17
			</span></i>: but, in earlier authors, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of the mind, <i>contentedness, good temper</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Alc.</u>
				1.122c
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀλιγόδεια καὶ εὐ</span>.
				<i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.457
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> of the body,
				<i>ease and lightness in moving</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐ. καὶ εὐχέρεια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					942d
				</span></i>
			: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐ. πρὸς τὴν ποίησιν</span>
			<i>facility</i> in verse-making, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Cic.</u>
				40
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐ. πρήξιος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					7.694
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Adaeus</span>).</div>
